Package: hairline
Title: Clean, Predictable Figures for Medical and Data Science
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nikolas", "Schrader", email = "hi@nikolasschrader.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-4616-3804"))
Description: A design system for 'ggplot2' figures: one frame for titles, legends,
    panels and captions, a fixed spacing and type scale, colour-vision checked
    palettes, brand files in the 'brand.yml' format, and print-ready export.
    Produces output matching the 'hairline' Python package.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/schradern/hairline
BugReports: https://github.com/schradern/hairline/issues
Copyright: The bundled 'Hairline Sans' font is a modified Public Sans,
        Copyright 2015 The Public Sans Project Authors, under the SIL
        Open Font License 1.1; see inst/COPYRIGHTS.
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3)
Imports: S7, ggplot2 (>= 4.0.0), grid, grDevices, jsonlite, ragg,
        rlang, systemfonts, textshaping, tools, utils, yaml
Suggests: cowplot, metafor, patchwork, png, rsvg, survival, svglite,
        testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
